Subject: narrow the URL pill to the reference's width

380 DIP rather than 460. Measured from the reference's fullscreen capture the
pill is about 345; at 460 in a modest window it read as filling the toolbar,
which the operator called out as "full width".

Why: operator feedback on the first DMG.
Removable when: never; it is one number and the parameter stays sweepable.
---
 chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc
index 68b6ff2441bf9..8b83052903bd4 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kToolbarButtonHeight, &kArcStyleWindow,
                    "toolbar_button_height", 28);
 
 BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kLocationBarWidth, &kArcStyleWindow,
-                   "location_bar_width", 460);
+                   "location_bar_width", 380);
 
 BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(bool, kOpenCommandBarForTesting, &kArcStyleWindow,
                    "open_command_bar", false);
